# Arrowing down the settings categories. Each press must announce the item you
# landed on and where it sits — never the one you left.
#
# Reported on hardware: pressing Down read "general. speech, 2 of 7", then
# "speech. keyboard, 3 of 7". The previous item first, then the current one.
#
# FocusTracker had an exemption letting through any announcement about an
# element it had never seen hold focus, meant to keep alerts audible. A focus
# event the provider deduped away never reached the tracker, so the stale
# announcement about the item just left looked unfamiliar and was spoken. The
# exemption is gone: a focus or selection announcement about something that is
# not the focus is stale, and there is no case where it is not.
#
# Alerts stay audible because they are never given a predicate at all — see
# an-alert-survives-a-focus-change.

node c1 ListItem "General"  pos=1 size=7
node c2 ListItem "Speech"   pos=2 size=7
node c3 ListItem "Keyboard" pos=3 size=7
focus c1
drain
focus c2
select c2
drain
focus c3
select c3

expect
  General, list item, 1 of 7
  Speech, list item, 2 of 7
  Keyboard, list item, 3 of 7
